  "worked_solution": "Notice that every point on the graph $y=g(x)$ is two units *to the right* and six units *up* of the corresponding point on the graph of $y=f(x).$ \n\nSo, we conclude that $g(x)=f(x-2)+6,$ and therefore $a=-2$ and $b=6.$",
